WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.378
AI engineering moves fast, and the useful parts are scattered.

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:07.940
Across whitepapers, engineering blogs and repos.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.622
Second Brain OS collects them into one path we can follow.

00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:16.335
A course on building agents:

00:00:16.385 --> 00:00:18.636
seven modules, from a single prompt to a production agent.

00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:21.838
Five handbooks that go deep on one layer each.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.533
A hands-on project:

00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:29.096
a second brain, a knowledge base an agent builds and maintains in plain markdown.

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:32.898
And the links worth our time, each one checked at the source.

00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:39.838
Theory with sources, a build in every module, and a reading list where every entry has a reason to be here.

00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:46.238
New to building agents? Start with What an agent is, then the course in order.

00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:52.344
One layer of your agent hurting? Open its handbook. Want a project to practise on?

00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:53.858
Build the second brain.

00:00:54.408 --> 00:00:59.982
That's Second Brain OS. Start with page one: What an agent is.
